      "text": "display: contents makes the element itself disappear from the box model, its own box is not rendered, but its children remain fully visible and participate in the layout as if they were direct children of the element's parent. Useful for wrapper <div>s that you need in the HTML for semantic or scripting reasons but don't want to affect your grid or flex layout."
