      "html": "The <strong><code>aspect-ratio</code></strong> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS\" target=\"_blank\">CSS</a> property allows you to define the desired width-to-height ratio of an element's box. This means that even if the parent container or viewport size changes, the browser will adjust the element's dimensions to maintain the specified width-to-height ratio. The specified <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/aspect ratio\" target=\"_blank\">aspect ratio</a> is used in the calculation of auto sizes and some other layout functions.",
      "text": "The aspect-ratio CSS property allows you to define the desired width-to-height ratio of an element's box. This means that even if the parent container or viewport size changes, the browser will adjust the element's dimensions to maintain the specified width-to-height ratio. The specified aspect ratio is used in the calculation of auto sizes and some other layout functions."
