      "text": "In the old days of HTML, the <i> element was used to italicize text. But today in the era of HTML5 this element has a newer semantic meaning. It is used to imply idiomatic text, technical terms and other taxonomical designations. It will still italicize the text, but if all you want is that stylistic change you should apply the CSS font-style property to something like a span element instead to avoid implying other semantic meanings."
