      "html": "<p>The <strong><code>&lt;defs&gt;</code></strong> element is used to store graphical objects that will be used at a later time. Objects created inside a <code>&lt;defs&gt;</code> element are not rendered directly. To display them you have to reference them (with a <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Element/use\" target=\"_blank\">use</a> element for example).</p>\n<p>Graphical objects can be referenced from anywhere, however, defining these objects inside of a <code>&lt;defs&gt;</code> element promotes understandability of the SVG content and is beneficial to the overall accessibility of the document. To learn more visit this <a href=\"https://svg-tutorial.com/forest\" target=\"_blank\">SVG tutorial</a>.</p>\n",
